<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch8-chapter-ci-1m1p" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Confidence Intervals</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> This chapter solidifies the idea of parameter estimation, introducing confidence intervals. The focus is on confidence intervals for one
       mean and for one proportion. 
      Students learn how to interpret confidence intervals and pay attention to effect size and practical importance. They also learn the 
      effect of sample size and confidence level on the width of the confidence interval. There is also a discussion on precision and bias.
      The chapter ends with students learning how to make a decision about a hypothesis test using a confidence interval and how the two inference methods complement each other.
    </p>
  </introduction>



  <objectives>
    <ol>
    <li>Explore...</li>

    <li>Learn...</li>

    <li>Understand...</li>

    <li>Apply...</li>
  </ol>
  </objectives>


  

